      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The lateral surface area of the pyramid consists of 4 triangles with base 10 cm and height 12 cm each. The area of each triangle is (1/2) * base * height = (1/2) * 10 * 12 = 60 square cm. So the total area of the 4 triangles is 4 * 60 = 240 square cm.\nWe can also use Heron's formula to find the slant height of each triangle. Using the Pythagorean Theorem, we find that the slant height is √(10^2 + 12^2) = 13.86 cm.\nThe area of each triangle is also (1/2) * base * slant height = (1/2) * 10 * 13.86 = 69.3 cm^2. So the total area of the 4 triangles is 4 * 69.3 = 277.2 square cm.\nAdding up the area of the square base (10^2 = 100 square cm) and the area of the lateral surface (240 + 277.2 = 517.2 square cm), we find that the total surface area of the pyramid is 100 + 517.2 = 617.2 square cm.",
